<cell>A bead is made from material with constant density
7 grams per cubic millimeter 
by drilling a cylindrical hole
of radius 1 mm through a sphere of radius 
4 mm.
(a) Set up a triple integral in cylindrical 
coordinates representing the mass of the
bead in grams (do not include units).  If necessary,
enter <m>\theta</m> as <em>theta.</em>
<CENTER><m>\displaystyle \iiint\limits_{Bead} f \, dV
=
\int_A^B \!\! \int_C^D \!\! \int_E^F \!\!</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/> <m>dz \, dr \, d\theta</m></CENTER>
